'''Michael D'Andrea Carter''' (born October 29, 1960) is an American former professional [[American football|football]] player and [[track and field]] athlete. He played pro football as a [[nose tackle]] with the [[San Francisco 49ers]] in the [[National Football League]] (NFL). Carter was a three-time [[Pro Bowl]] and four-time [[All-Pro]] selection, including three times on the first-team. He helped the 49ers win three [[Super Bowl]]s. He was also an [[Olympic Games|Olympic]] athlete, winning a [[silver medal]] in the [[shot put]] in the [[1984 Summer Olympics]].
